From 6fe4cd7876953d5b7f7e4f295ec88f104f08e9a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:46:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc/webui: v1.2.9 - QoS v4: per-class WRR weights + L4S flag;
 group shaper objects dropped with cause

- rc/qos.c start_hwqos_classful: new qos_sched nvram (5 tokens by queue
  position: p = strict priority, w<1-63> = WRR weight). Weighted classes get
  tmctl setqcfg --schedmode 2 --weight N, emitted BEFORE setqdropalg/
  setqshaper (config-rewriting verbs first - the v1 ordering lesson), with
  the platform-tuned qsize read back at run time and preserved (setqcfg is
  skipped if the read fails; never write a zero qsize). qos_l4s=1
  (EXPERIMENTAL, default 0) adds --l4s 1 on every class queue - DualPI2
  ECT(1) marking for L4S-capable flows, inert if a flow/TM rejects it.
  Stop branch restores schedmode 1 (weight 1 = lowest legal value, ignored
  in SP; the tool rejects weight 0) and --l4s 0 on any queue the script
  reconfigured. With no weighted class and L4S off the generated script is
  byte-identical to v3.
- shared/defaults.c: qos_sched default "p,p,p,p,p" (CKN_STR64), qos_l4s
  default "0".
- www/Reaper_QoS.asp: class editor gains Mode (Priority/Weighted) + Weight
  columns with weighted-pool queue notes; serialize writes qos_sched and
  enforces WRR contiguity at the bottom (an SP row below the pool would
  silently outrank it). L4S toggle (EXPERIMENTAL tag). FAQ: Priority-vs-
  Weighted, L4S explainer, and the group-cap recipe.

GROUP SHAPER OBJECTS / ORL: DROPPED with cause. tmctl CreateShaper returns
an object POINTER that SetShaperQueue consumes, but the CLI never prints it
on success -> not scriptable; libtmctl.so ships no headers and rc has no
tmctl linkage, so the C route is undocumented-blob guesswork. ORL is
redundant with the v3 port shaper (both whole-port aggregate caps). The
group-cap outcome = member ceilings summing to the group budget under the
aggregate cap (+ weights for fair sharing) - documented in the FAQ.

Mock-validated render. EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.2.9. Metal tests owed: weighted
pool shares by weight under dual bulk saturation while SP classes stay
first; getqcfg shows schedMode 2/weight after apply and schedMode 1 after
stop; qsize preserved across apply; L4S toggle accepted by setqcfg (or
fails inert); v3 regression pass (port shaper/minrates/DSCP/stats).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
